Package: skycue
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, adduser, diffutils
Recommends: python3, python3-pil, curl, unzip
Suggests: readsb, dump978-fa, gdal-bin, python3-gdal
Description: ADS-B and UAT operator console and forwarding bridge
 skycue runs beside the reader's receiver stack (readsb for 1090 MHz,
 dump978 for 978 MHz UAT) and reads the decoded traffic those programs
 already publish. It does not feed, replace or configure them: no decoder
 is a dependency, and nothing here edits their configuration or restarts
 them.
 .
 The skycued daemon serves an offline web console with a map, a traffic
 table and alerts, and sends cues to cue clients. Map tiles and
 overlays are made on the machine with skycue-make-maps (needs GDAL or a
 container runtime). The service is enabled but not started on install:
 set receiver lat and lon in /etc/skycue/skycue.toml first, then
 run "systemctl enable --now skycued".

Package: libskycue-dev
Architecture: any
Section: libdevel
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, libboost-system-dev
Description: skycue client library (static) and CMake package
 libskycue is the static C++ client library for skycued's cue interface,
 with its headers and a CMake package configuration for
 find_package(skycue).
 .
 skycue runs beside the reader's receiver stack and does not feed,
 replace or configure it; this package only lets a client program talk to
 skycued.
